":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"DirectedHypergraph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedhypergraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A directed hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordered pair of vertex sets, its sources (tail) and its targets (head). Gallo, Longo, Pallottino","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and Nguyen, “Directed hypergraphs and applications”, ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discrete Applied Mathematics"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"42(2–3):177–201, 1993, define a hyperarc as “an ordered pair … of (possibly empty) disjoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subsets”; here either side may be empty and a vertex may be on both, the hypergraph form of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop (XGI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiHypergraph"},{"text":" allows both).","type":"text"}]},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Extensions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Extensions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"Extensions to BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-bidirectionaldirectedgraph-extensions"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-DirectedHypergraph-Extensions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-DirectedHyper